# Per-board repo version overrides for jetson-agx-thor.
#
# Sourced by bootstrap.sh after the default URL_*/SRCREV_* values are set
# (from scripts/upstream-repos.env), but before the repos[] array is built.
#
# === BLACKSAIL / JetPack 7.2 / L4T R39.2.0 EXPERIMENT (feature/jp7.2-support) ===
# Thor is the canary for unifying all three Jetson boards onto JetPack 7.2.
# The JP7.2 line is the first to support both the Orin family AND Thor
# simultaneously (per meta-tegra's
# docs/release-notes/JetPack-7.2-L4T-R39.2.0-Notes.md), and it declares
# LAYERSERIES_COMPAT = "blacksail" — the in-development Yocto series after
# wrynose (6.0). So the whole stack moves to blacksail-era pins.
#
# That work arrived on the wip-l4t-r39.2.0 branch, which OE4T has since
# rebased into master and deleted. master now carries both the R39.2 release
# notes and LAYERSERIES_COMPAT_tegra = "blacksail", so the meta-tegra* pins
# below track master. There is no r39.2 release branch yet; OE4T cuts those as
# master-l4t-rXX.Y.x, so move to master-l4t-r39.2.x when it appears.
# scripts/ext/check-jp7.2-upstream.sh watches for both.
#
# This is an EXPERIMENT to find what breaks: blacksail is a moving dev target
# and several layers (meta-openembedded, meta-virtualization) have NOT yet
# declared blacksail compatibility upstream. We bridge that with gated
# LAYERSERIES_COMPAT:append overrides in
# conf/template/include/local/blacksail-compat.inc (required from local.conf).
#
# Isolation: WENDYOS_LAYER_TREE="blacksail" makes bootstrap.sh clone every
# upstream repo under repos/blacksail/ — parallel to repos/wrynose/ (the
# validated r38.4/JP7.1 Thor fallback on main) and repos/scarthgap/ (Orin/
# RPi/QEMU). The validated trees are never touched; revert = git checkout main.
#
# All SRCREVs below were re-resolved from upstream HEADs on 2026-08-04
# (git ls-remote); the previous set dated from 2026-06-15. Pinned for
# reproducibility since blacksail/master move.
#
# Why the whole set moved at once: oe-core gained an SPDX license-expression
# parser on 2026-07-15, and both OE4T layers converted their recipes from the
# old "&" syntax to SPDX "AND" a week later. Against the 2026-06-15 oe-core
# those recipes fail to parse — "LICENSE value ... has an invalid format".
# So meta-tegra could not move on its own; and moving oe-core on its own would
# have left meta-openembedded and meta-virtualization seven weeks behind the
# core classes they build against, trading one skew for another. No upstream
# layer has cut a blacksail release branch yet, so master HEAD is still the
# only target available.
WENDYOS_LAYER_TREE="blacksail"

# Split-poky composition on blacksail. oe-core master declares
# LAYERSERIES_CORENAMES = "wrynose blacksail" and LAYERSERIES_COMPAT_core =
# "blacksail"; meta-yocto master + bitbake master (2.19.0, >= oe-core's
# BB_MIN_VERSION 2.18.0) match it.
SRCREV_BITBAKE="c870f5bd96ad02efc02c58133c27bdae3a300e3e"
SRCREV_OECORE="2faf8e366df74aded7898904b72317521a08e2f6"
SRCREV_METAYOCTO="9c6cf36c3511b94957aba04002d98bec665e9f1e"

# meta-openembedded master HEAD. NOTE: master still declares
# LAYERSERIES_COMPAT = "whinlatter wrynose" (NOT blacksail) as of 2026-08-04
# — bridged via blacksail-compat.inc. Re-pin to an upstream commit that
# declares blacksail once meta-oe bumps, then drop the override.
SRCREV_OE="0a60011ec174b91104a110c353cbf18748951270"

# meta-virtualization master HEAD. Same situation: master declares
# LAYERSERIES_COMPAT = "wrynose" only — bridged via blacksail-compat.inc.
SRCREV_VIRT="526c97254fe43e0924df034aaa825f33ec30407c"

# meta-tegra master (JetPack 7.2 / L4T R39.2.0, Thor + Orin family).
# conf/layer.conf declares LAYERSERIES_COMPAT_tegra = "blacksail".
#
# Re-pinned 2026-08-04 from d0b2f4d81dc3, which lived on the deleted
# wip-l4t-r39.2.0 branch. A commit that no upstream ref can reach breaks the
# Thor CI build: bootstrap.sh's bulk `git fetch origin` cannot deliver it, so
# a warm repo cache fails outright, and a cold clone survives only through the
# fetch-by-SHA fallback for as long as GitHub still serves the dangling
# object. Nearest master-side equivalent of the old pin is ceb73c72 — keep it
# as the fallback if master HEAD misbehaves on Thor. It is reachable from
# master, so unlike d0b2f4d81dc3 it stays a durable pin.
SRCREV_TEGRA="de0a5a233d4e5aff0ed64da39aeec9310ce693c9"

# meta-tegra-community master; conf/layer.conf declares
# LAYERSERIES_COMPAT_tegra-community = "blacksail". LAYERDEPENDS pulls in
# openembedded-layer + meta-python, which is why those must be made
# blacksail-compatible (see blacksail-compat.inc).
#
# Re-pinned 2026-08-04 from 931db8c0f56e for the same reason. Fallback: 98d9e63.
SRCREV_TEGRA_COMM="f0beedf81977fe6cd28f39912c53139290f5a6f4"

# OTA-related SRCREVs are left at their upstream defaults — Thor uses the
# wendyos-update OTA stack (WENDYOS_OTA = "wendy").
